cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata from this file."
type: software
title: "LenticulumLM: a diffusion language model assembled from implicit learners"
version: "20261015-proto"
authors:
  - name: "MathStruct"
    website: "https://mathstruct.org"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/MathStruct/LenticulumLM"
url: "https://mathstruct.org/LenticulumLM/"
keywords:
  - diffusion language models
  - implicit learning
  - products of experts
  - factor graphs
  - Julia
abstract: >-
  LenticulumLM assembles a diffusion language model from implicit learners. Each
  part is a relation over a few token positions, the model is their product, and
  every query, whether continuation, backward prediction or infilling, is answered
  by root finding with the known tokens clamped. It builds on Lenticulum.jl, which
  provides the implicit learners, their products and their beliefs.
